.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt 0VERBS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm 0verbs
.Nd search OpenBSD and NetBSD package indexes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl eFjuv
.Op Fl \-os Ar os
.Op Fl \-release Ar release
.Op Fl \-arch Ar arch
.Op Fl \-mirror Ar url
.Op Fl \-cache-dir Ar dir
.Op Fl \-limit Ar n
.Op Fl \-max-age Ar days
.Op Fl \-timeout Ar seconds
.Op Fl \-list-releases
.Op Fl \-clean
.Op Fl \-sha256 | Fl \-sha512
.Op Fl \-url
.Op Fl \-installed
.Op Fl \-installed-only
.Op Fl \-newest
.Op Fl \-no-suggest
.Op Ar package ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
searches the package indexes published by
.Ox
and
.Nx .
Indexes are downloaded once, cached, and reused.
By default, cached data is used whenever it is available; the network is
contacted only when the cache is missing or when
.Fl \-update
is given.
.Pp
Each
.Ar package
argument is a case-insensitive word.
A package must contain every word.
A word containing any of
.Ql ^$*?()[]{}|\e
is treated as an ECMAScript regular expression; other words are matched
literally.
Use
.Fl F
to force literal matching for every word.
.Pp
Unless
.Fl \-release
is given, the newest cached release for the selected operating system and
architecture is used.
If no release is cached, the latest release is discovered on the mirror.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.It Fl \-version
Print the program version and exit.
.It Fl \-os Ar os
Select the package universe.
.Ar os
must be
.Cm openbsd
or
.Cm netbsd .
If omitted, the operating system is detected with
.Xr uname 3 ;
systems other than
.Ox
are treated as
.Nx .
.It Fl \-release Ar release
Search the specified release.
Valid forms include
.Ar 7.8 ,
.Ar snapshots ,
and
.Ar 10.0_2026Q3 .
If the release is not cached, or if
.Fl \-update
is used, its indexes are downloaded.
Without this option, the newest cached release is used, or the latest release
is discovered from the mirror when the cache is empty.
.It Fl \-arch Ar arch
Use the specified package architecture, for example
.Ar amd64
or
.Ar x86_64 .
Architecture names are normalized between the names reported by
.Xr uname 3
and the names used on the mirrors.
The default is the current machine architecture.
.It Fl \-list-releases
List release names.
Cached releases are listed unless
.Fl \-update
is given, in which case the mirror is queried.
If no releases are cached, the mirror is queried.
With
.Fl j ,
the output is a JSON array of strings.
.It Fl u , Fl \-update
Refresh cached package indexes from the mirror.
If
.Fl \-release
is not given, the latest release is discovered from the mirror.
When used without a search word and without
.Fl \-list-releases ,
the indexes are refreshed and
.Nm
exits.
When search words are present, the indexes are refreshed and the search is
performed afterwards.
.It Fl \-mirror Ar url
Use
.Ar url
as the package mirror instead of the default.
The URL must begin with
.Ql http://
or
.Ql https:// .
For
.Ox ,
the default mirror is read from
.Pa /etc/installurl ;
if that file is missing or invalid, the public CDN mirror is used.
For
.Nx ,
the default is the public CDN pkgsrc mirror.
.It Fl \-cache-dir Ar dir
Store cached indexes under
.Ar dir
instead of the default cache directory.
A leading
.Ql ~
is expanded to the home directory.
Trailing slashes are removed.
.It Fl \-clean
Remove the cache directory and exit.
For safety, the directory must live beneath the default cache root or be named
.Ql 0verbs .
.It Fl \-sha256 , Fl \-sha512
Show each package's digest in text output.
The digest type is determined by the backend: SHA256 for
.Ox
and SHA512 for
.Nx .
Both options are equivalent aliases.
JSON output always includes the digest.
.It Fl \-url
Show each package's download URL in text output.
JSON output always includes the URL.
.It Fl j , Fl \-json
Write machine-readable JSON to standard output.
Progress and diagnostic messages are written to standard error.
See
.Sx JSON OUTPUT .
.It Fl \-limit Ar n
Show at most
.Ar n
results after matching, de-duplication, and newest-version selection.
.Ar n
must be at least 1.
.It Fl \-installed
Mark packages that are installed locally.
Installed packages are read from the system package database.
Matching ignores the version: an installed
.Pa firefox-149.0
marks an available
.Pa firefox-150.0
as installed.
In text output the package is followed by
.Ql [installed] ;
in JSON output the
.Va installed
field is true.
.It Fl \-installed-only
Show only package lines that are installed locally.
This implies
.Fl \-installed
and collapses each package line to its newest available version.
.It Fl \-newest
Show only the newest version of each package line.
For
.Ox ,
flavors are kept separate and the line is based on the major version, or on
the major and minor versions for projects with a major version below 10.
For
.Nx ,
one row per package stem is shown.
.It Fl \-max-age Ar days
Warn on standard error when the cached index is older than
.Ar days .
The default is 7.
A value of 0 disables the warning.
.It Fl \-timeout Ar seconds
Set the network timeout in seconds.
The default is 120.
.Ar seconds
must be at least 1.
.It Fl e , Fl \-exact
Match whole package names or package stems instead of searching for
substrings.
This also shows only the newest version of each matching line.
.It Fl F , Fl \-fixed-strings
Treat every search word as a literal string, even if it contains characters
that would otherwise be interpreted as a regular expression.
.It Fl \-no-suggest
Do not print
.Dq Did you mean?
suggestions when a search has no matches.
.It Fl v , Fl \-verbose
Print extra diagnostics to standard error.
.It Cm \-\-
End option processing.
All following arguments are treated as search words.
.It Ar package
One or more case-insensitive words that must all occur in a package name.
If no search word is supplied, the program exits with an error unless
.Fl \-update ,
.Fl \-list-releases ,
.Fl \-clean ,
.Fl h ,
or
.Fl \-version
is used.
.El
.Sh CACHE-FIRST BEHAVIOR
Searches read cached indexes and do not contact the network when a cache is
present.
The network is used in the following cases:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
No cached index exists for the selected release and architecture.
.It
.Fl \-update
is given.
.It
.Fl \-list-releases
is used and no releases are cached.
.El
.Pp
Without
.Fl \-release ,
the newest cached release is selected.
If nothing is cached, the latest release is discovered from the mirror.
With
.Fl \-update
and no
.Fl \-release ,
the mirror is asked for the latest release.
.Pp
The first run for a release therefore requires either a network connection or a
populated cache.
Use
.Fl \-update
to fetch fresh indexes; cached data is used automatically at all other times.
.Sh JSON OUTPUT
With
.Fl j ,
.Nm
writes a single JSON object to standard output.
The top-level fields are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va os
The selected operating system,
.Ql openbsd
or
.Ql netbsd .
.It Va release
The selected release.
.It Va arch
The normalized architecture.
.It Va count
The number of returned packages.
.It Va packages
An array of package objects.
.It Va suggestions
An optional array of suggested package stems, present when the search had no
matches and suggestions were generated.
.El
.Pp
Each package object contains:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va name
The full package name, including version and flavor.
.It Va version
The parsed version, or
.Ql null
if the name could not be parsed.
.It Va flavor
The flavor suffix, or
.Ql null .
.It Va hash_type
The digest type, either
.Ql sha256
or
.Ql sha512 .
.It Va hash
The package digest.
.It Va url
The package download URL.
.It Va branch
.Ql stable
for entries from
.Pa packages-stable
on
.Ox ,
otherwise
.Ql null .
.It Va installed
A boolean indicating whether the package line is installed locally.
.El
.Pp
.Fl \-list-releases Fl j
prints a JSON array of release names instead of an object.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A search that returns no matches is not an error.
Diagnostics and the
.Dq No matches found.
message are written to standard error.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/installurl
Default
.Ox
mirror URL, when present.
.It Pa $XDG_CACHE_HOME/0verbs
Cache directory when
.Ev XDG_CACHE_HOME
is set.
.It Pa ~/.cache/0verbs
Default cache directory otherwise.
.It Pa ~/.cache/0verbs/openbsd/<release>/packages/<arch>/SHA256
Cached
.Ox
package index.
.It Pa ~/.cache/0verbs/openbsd/<release>/packages-stable/<arch>/SHA256
Cached
.Ox
stable package index.
.It Pa ~/.cache/0verbs/netbsd/<release>/packages/<arch>/SHA512.bz2
Cached compressed
.Nx
index.
.It Pa ~/.cache/0verbs/netbsd/<release>/packages/<arch>/SHA512
Decompressed and cleaned
.Nx
index used for searching.
.It Pa /var/db/pkg
.Ox
package database, also checked on
.Nx .
.It Pa /usr/pkg/pkgdb
.Nx
package database.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for the cache.
The cache is stored in
.Pa $XDG_CACHE_HOME/0verbs .
.It Ev HOME
Used to locate the default cache directory when
.Ev XDG_CACHE_HOME
is not set.
.It Ev USERPROFILE
Fallback home directory on systems that do not set
.Ev HOME .
.It Ev http_proxy , https_proxy , no_proxy
Standard proxy variables honored by libcurl.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Search the newest cached release:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ 0verbs firefox
.Ed
.Pp
Show the newest patch of each exact PHP line, with digests:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ 0verbs -e php --newest --sha256
.Ed
.Pp
Search NetBSD and emit JSON:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ 0verbs --os netbsd --json --limit 20 jdk
.Ed
.Pp
Refresh the cache, then search:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ 0verbs --update firefox
.Ed
.Pp
Refresh and list releases from the mirror:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ 0verbs --update --list-releases
.Ed
.Pp
Show only installed package lines:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ 0verbs --installed-only firefox
.Ed
.Pp
Search for a literal string containing regular-expression characters:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ 0verbs -F 'c++'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkg_add 1 ,
.Xr pkg_info 1 ,
.Xr pkgin 1 ,
.Xr curl 1 ,
.Xr bzip2 1
